# TODO: Verification Plan for Incremental ML-KEM-768 Functions

## Overview

This document describes the TODO plan for verifying the functions and constants
listed in [`doc/truong/incremental_mlkem768_functions.txt`](../truong/incremental_mlkem768_functions.txt),
which enumerates all fully qualified function and constant names from
`src/incremental_mlkem768.rs` (Rust source). These are extracted into
`Spqr/Code/Funs.lean` (Lean 4 / Aeneas extraction).

All extractable functions are configured via
[`aeneas-config.yml`](../../aeneas-config.yml). Functions not appearing in
that configuration (e.g. `#[cfg(test)]` or `#[hax_lib::opaque]` items) are
either not extracted or emitted as axioms and therefore cannot be fully
verified in the current framework.

The current Lean specification tree for the incremental ML-KEM-768 layer
lives at
[`Spqr/Specs/IncrementalMlkem768/`](../../Spqr/Specs/IncrementalMlkem768/)
and is grounded by external (opaque) function models in
[`Spqr/Code/FunsExternal.lean`](../../Spqr/Code/FunsExternal.lean).

