## 0. External (Opaque) Function Models — Statistics and Analysis

The incremental ML-KEM-768 module operates over opaque cryptographic
primitives provided by the upstream `libcrux_ml_kem` crate. Unlike the
polynomial or GF(2¹⁶) layers, there is no internal mathematical
foundation to verify — the module's correctness reduces to
*byte-length preservation* through opaque cryptographic calls. All
external models are consolidated in
[`Spqr/Code/FunsExternal.lean`](../../Spqr/Code/FunsExternal.lean).

