## 6. Background Knowledge for Specification Theorem Properties

The specification theorems in the incremental ML-KEM-768 layer are
principally **byte-length preservation** theorems: they verify that
each function's output byte vectors have the exact lengths specified
by the Rust `#[hax_lib::ensures]` annotations. The following
background knowledge supports the derivation of the full properties
of these specification theorems.

